<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Stiklestad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1030">1030</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Stiklestad was fought on 29 July 1030 in Trøndelag, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, where King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-ii-of-norway">Olaf Haraldsson</a>, returning from exile to reclaim his throne, was killed by an army of Norwegian farmers and chieftains loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great">Cnut the Great</a>. Olaf was soon venerated as a saint, and his cult as Saint Olaf, Norway's eternal king, helped establish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and royal authority in the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-stiklestad.jpg" alt="Battle of Stiklestad" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Nicolai Arbo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arbo-Olav_den_helliges_fall_i_slaget_p%C3%A5_Stiklestad_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
